WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.320
The course can be summarized as a practical operating routine.

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.680
First, define the claim and the decision.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.520
What is being asserted, who needs to act,

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.955
and what could go wrong if the organization acts too quickly or too slowly?

00:00:10.955 --> 00:00:13.935
This step prevents the review from becoming an open-ended debate.

00:00:13.935 --> 00:00:17.770
It ties evidence collection to the decision the organization actually has to make.

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:20.600
Second, preserve context and evaluate the source.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.665
Capture the artifact, surrounding records, time window, collection method,

00:00:23.665 --> 00:00:26.020
and chain of custody details that matter.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:29.535
Ask whether the source is reliable over time and whether the specific information is

00:00:29.535 --> 00:00:30.920
credible in this case.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.960
Provenance is often the difference between a useful artifact and a persuasive object with

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:35.760
uncertain meaning.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.305
Third, verify evidence and test alternatives.

00:00:38.305 --> 00:00:40.400
Look for independent corroboration where possible.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.100
Check whether timestamps, identity context, system records, approval paths,

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.360
and telemetry support the same conclusion.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:49.315
Write down assumptions and ask what else could explain the evidence.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:52.760
Inconsistency deserves attention, but the answer may be benign error,

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:55.840
incomplete collection, or process drift rather than deception.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:59.160
Finally, communicate in decision-ready language and improve the system.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.400
Separate facts, assumptions, and judgments.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.600
Use confidence language that fits the evidence.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.140
Escalate through the right ownership path, document what was preserved and why,

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:10.640
and avoid spreading sensitive or misleading material unnecessarily.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.290
After the review, update playbooks, trusted channel lists, approval workflows,

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:15.000
and training.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.200
Counter-deception becomes valuable when it is repeatable under pressure.
